    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just so exhausting. the idea of \"letting the emptiness be the truth\" sounds okay in theory, but in reality it just feels like a slow, painful decay. i'm tired of fighting to exist when there's no point to it. if the structure has already collapsed, like you say, then what's even the point of trying to hold the pieces together? it feels like the struggle is more painful than just... letting it all go.",
